--- RENDER SMOKE: real Bucharest 1:1 bbox, 16 regions, cached tiles ---
Four runs, sequential (the first attempt launched all four
concurrently because PowerShell does not wait for a GUI-subsystem
exe — Start-Process -Wait fixed it; concurrent runs also starved the
old binary into producing nothing).

  A 3.1.4 merged exe, caves, seed 11   block_hash=1cca84f4149678e4
  B 3.1.4 merged exe, caves, seed 11   block_hash=1cca84f4149678e4
  C 3.1.4 merged exe, no caves         block_hash=229fbe0efcc1076f  114,438,144 bytes
  D 3.1.2 shipped exe, no caves        block_hash=229fbe0efcc1076f  121,425,920 bytes

A==B: the FnvHashSet determinism fix holds in the merged binary.
C==D: the merged binary places every block exactly where the shipped
3.1.2 did on the non-cave path. Confirmed past the hash by decoding
r.0.0.mca from both to per-position block names: 1024/1024 chunks
identical, 0 differing blocks of 1,391,661. (Byte- or palette-level
comparison is noise — the triage run's control already proved the
parallel merge reorders palettes between identical runs; A and B
differ by 32 KB on disk while hashing identical.)
C is 5.75% smaller than D: the triage agent's block-light saving,
alive and working inside our merged binary.
Caves intentionally excluded from the cross-version pair: 3.1.4's
reproducibility fix shifts cave layout once relative to 3.1.2, which
is documented behaviour, not a regression.

